More than 1,030 people have died from an Ebola outbreak declared in May in the Democratic Republic of Congo and Uganda, the World Health Organization said on Wednesday, as confirmed cases in the DRC surpassed 2,530, according to government data.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">75b61aee-866f-11f1-893a-5ba20fd9084b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 09:51:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg">AP Photo/Dirole Lotsima Dieudonn - Dirole Lotsima Dieudonne</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>United States announces landmark civilian nuclear deal with Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260722-saudi-nuclear-deal-set-to-bypass-iaea-s-toughest-inspections-regime</link><description>
The United States on Wednesday announced a deal with Saudi Arabia that would establish a civilian nuclear programme in the Gulf country, with Washington insisting the agreement includes nonproliferation safeguards.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eaf8cb8c-85be-11f1-9267-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2227026692.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eaf8cb8c-85be-11f1-9267-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2227026692.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">217dce1e-85bf-11f1-a1db-db1171cf99df</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 12:46:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eaf8cb8c-85be-11f1-9267-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2227026692.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - SCOTT OLSON</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron talks environment minister out of quitting over pesticide U-turn</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260722-france-environment-minister-barbut-quits-then-stays-to-act-on-climate</link><description>
France's environment minister, Monique Barbut, will remain in her post, given the "urgency" to act on climate change, after submitting her resignation to President Emmanuel Macron over a bill to reintroduce bee-harming pesticides, her team said Wednesday.
