French mining group Eramet is considering a major expansion of manganese processing in Gabon under an agreement that could strengthen the country’s industrial base, modernise its railway network and reduce its reliance on exports of unprocessed ore.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a5bbb926-8488-11f1-9289-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201639434838.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a5bbb926-8488-11f1-9289-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201639434838.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f66a1f82-84f8-11f1-b95b-159cb199153e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 08:52:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a5bbb926-8488-11f1-9289-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201639434838.jpg">© Ludovic Marin / Pool AFP via AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Germany looks to Azerbaijan as Armenia ties shift regional relationships</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260722-germany-looks-to-azerbaijan-as-armenia-ties-shift-the-regional-map</link><description>
German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and Azerbaijani President Ilham Aliyev have signed a series of economic agreements aimed at deepening Berlin's access to Baku's gas reserves and transit routes. The deal comes as Germany works to diversify its energy supply, and as Azerbaijan balances a Europe-leaning Armenia against a recently repaired relationship with Moscow.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/419cc27e-8509-11f1-9cd9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2QJ4YJ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/419cc27e-8509-11f1-9cd9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2QJ4YJ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b96ba18a-84e1-11f1-a40b-5172daa12d9e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 05:08:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/419cc27e-8509-11f1-9cd9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2QJ4YJ.jpg">AFP - TOBIAS SCHWARZ</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France’s emergency agriculture bill passed, amid divisions over pesticides</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260721-france-s-emergency-agriculture-bill-passed-amid-divisions-over-pesticides</link><description>
France’s National Assembly has approved an emergency agriculture bill after a tense overnight debate, clearing the way for the possible temporary return of two pesticides banned in the country but still authorised elsewhere in the European Union.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1e944cd6-84df-11f1-80b0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2NT88R.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1e944cd6-84df-11f1-80b0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2NT88R.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c3cfa30-84d9-11f1-b6db-db2ffabab7f1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 19:07:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1e944cd6-84df-11f1-80b0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2NT88R.jpg">© AFP - DIMITAR DILKOFF </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France and Germany move to tackle EU’s growing trade deficit with China</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260721-france-and-germany-move-to-tackle-eu-s-growing-trade-deficit-with-china</link><description>
France and Germany are pressing for a stronger European Union response to China’s growing trade surplus and industrial overcapacity, as concerns mount over the impact on key European sectors.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ee530872-8205-11f1-bfc5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26198483233993.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ee530872-8205-11f1-bfc5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26198483233993.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2d0d434-842f-11f1-944b-131eff2948d7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 06:08:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ee530872-8205-11f1-bfc5-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26198483233993.jpg">Oliver Berg/DPA via AP - Oliver Berg</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Ukraine’s wartime unity put to the test by protests over military leadership</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260721-ukraine-s-wartime-unity-put-to-the-test-by-protests-over-military-leadership</link><description>
Protests over the dismissal of Ukraine’s reformist defence minister entered a fifth day on Monday, deepening a political crisis that has placed President Volodymyr Zelensky under mounting pressure to overhaul the country’s military leadership.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a11172da-84ce-11f1-bc50-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2PE3ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a11172da-84ce-11f1-bc50-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2PE3ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b2dc5c6e-84ce-11f1-abed-cba796d7c824</guid><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 07:33:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a11172da-84ce-11f1-bc50-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2PE3ZQ.jpg">AFP - GENYA SAVILOV</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight on Africa</category><title>Countdown to the ballot: Zambia gears up for August elections</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/spotlight-on-africa/20260721-countdown-to-the-ballot-zambia-gears-up-for-august-elections</link><description>
This week on Spotlight on Africa, we're heading to Zambia, where general elections are set to take place on the 13th August. Voters will go to the polls to elect a president, members of the National Assembly, councillors and council chairs. Incumbent President Hakainde Hichilema has already picked up endorsements from within his own camp, the UPND Alliance, the coalition that's held power since 2021. So what's at stake, and who's in the running?
